entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Mafikeng\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [284, 292]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mafikeng\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - Dec 6 . MOSCOW 1996-12-06 No weather-related closures of CIS airports are expected on December 7 and 8 , the Russian Weather Service said on Friday . -- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"MOSCOW\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [47, 53]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Skinheads attack Bratislava Rabbi - police . BRATISLAVA 1996-12-06 Four skinheads attacked and insulted the rabbi of Bratislava , Baruch Meyers , in the city centre on Friday , but he escaped unharmed , a police spokesman told Reuters . \\\" A group of four skinheads attacked the rabbi , one kicked him in the hand but caused no injury , \\\" the spokesman said . \\\" All four attackers were apprehended and two have been detained , \\\" the spokesman added He was unable to give more details . \\\" The further procedure is now in the hands of the local police investigator , \\\" the spokesman said . It was the second attack by skinheads in two years on Meyers , an American . Meyers was not available for comment .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Bratislava\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [17, 27]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bratislava\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"BRATISLAVA\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [45, 55]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bratislava\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Bratislava\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [117, 127]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bratislava\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Reuters\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [227, 234]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Reuters\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"American\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [653, 661]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Albanian jailed for threat of bomb suicide . TIRANA 1996-12-06 An Albanian court on Friday sentenced a man who threatened to blow himself up outside President Sali Berisha 's office to 13 years in jail for guerrilla action and illegal possession of arms . Buza last April said he would blow himself up outside the presidential palace unless he was allowed to speak to Berisha , who was at the time meeting Italian President Oscar Luigi Scalfaro . Buza was overpowered by riot police less than one hour after he began his action . \\\" Evaluating all the conditions of the case the court thinks the sentence should be lower than the minimum ( 15 years ) , \\\" Tirana judge Qazim Gjonaj added . The defendant denied the charges , saying his action was intended to urge the authorities to give him a $ 20,000 loan . Medical experts had concluded Buza was mentally unstable but fully responsible for the act he had committed , Gjonaj said .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Albanian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 8]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Albania\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"TIRANA\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [45, 51]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tirana\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Albanian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [66, 74]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Albania\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Sali Berisha\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [159, 171]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sali_Berisha\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Berisha\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [368, 375]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sali_Berisha\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Italian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [406, 413]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Oscar Luigi Scalfaro\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [424, 444]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oscar_Luigi_Scalfaro\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Tirana\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [654, 660]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tirana\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Polish ex-communist president to visit Pope . WARSAW 1996-12-06 Poland 's ex-communist President Aleksander Kwasniewski is likely to visit Polish-born Pope John Paul in early 1997 despite uneasy relations between the Vatican and Warsaw , the foreign minister said on Friday . \\\" President Kwasniewski plans to visit Italy on a invitation from President Oscar Scalfaro . A meeting with the Pope is also planned , \\\" Dariusz Rosati told a news conference . Rosati said that the atmosphere of the meeting , if it takes place , would largely depend on the progress in talks on ratification of a treaty between Warsaw and the Vatican . @ The ratification of the treaty , which was signed in 1993 by the then right-centrist government , is being delayed by an ex-communist party , which won parliamentary elections in the same year and now dominates parliament . The party , the Democratic Left Alliance , says the agreement would give the Catholic Church too much influence over life in Poland and could infringe on rights of other religious groups and non-believers . The relations with the Vatican have also been soured by a recent relaxation of Poland 's anti-abortion rules , which Kwasniewski signed into law last month .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Polish\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 6]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"WARSAW\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [46, 52]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Warsaw\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Poland\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [64, 70]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Aleksander Kwasniewski\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [97, 119]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aleksander_Kwa\\u015bniewski\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Vatican\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [217, 224]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vatican_City\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Warsaw\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [229, 235]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Warsaw\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Kwasniewski\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [288, 299]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aleksander_Kwa\\u015bniewski\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Italy\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [315, 320]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Oscar Scalfaro\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [352, 366]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oscar_Luigi_Scalfaro\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Dariusz Rosati\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [413, 427]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dariusz_Rosati\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Rosati\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [453, 459]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dariusz_Rosati\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Warsaw\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [604, 610]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Warsaw\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Vatican\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [619, 626]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vatican_City\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Democratic Left Alliance\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [871, 895]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Democratic_Left_Alliance\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Catholic Church\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [932, 947]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Catholic_Church\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Poland\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [980, 986]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Vatican\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1085, 1092]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vatican_City\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Poland\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1141, 1147]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Kwasniewski\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1179, 1190]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aleksander_Kwa\\u015bniewski\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Russia warns Norilsk , not expected to liquidate it . Lynnley Browning MOSCOW 1996-12-06 Russian Finance Minister Alexander Livshits warned financially-troubled Norilsk Nickel on Friday that it must pay overdue taxes , but analysts said the firm would not be liquidated or that its would assets would be frozen . \\\" Norilsk really is a big debtor , both to the federal and regional budgets , \\\" said Konstantin Chernyshev , equities analyst at Moscow brokerage Rinaco Plus and a Norilsk watcher . \\\" Livshits 's words are an attempt to put pressure on the company . \\\" The official Itar-Tass news agency quoted Livshits as telling parliamentary deputies that RAO Norilsky Nikel 0#NKEL.RUO had to pay its tax arrears and that bankruptcy procedures applied to the metals group . \\\" If it was an unsolicited statement and a bolt out of the blue , then it obviously means something , \\\" said Christopher Granville , chief economist at United City Bank in Moscow . \\\" But if it was a response to a deputy 's question that was essentially loaded , then it was the only answer he could have given . \\\" Russian tax and cabinet authorities , under pressure from the International Monetary Fund to boost tax revenues as a condition for receiving payments of a $ 10 billion , three-year loan to Moscow , have been striking fear into the hearts of some of Russia 's most prominent industrial firms by saying they must pay up or face liquidation . \\\" They could freeze metal , but it 's not a long-term solution to the problem and would n't put money in the budget , \\\" Chernyshev said . \\\" I do n't think they would do that . \\\" Entire social infrastructures in the icy Far North where Norilsk is based depend on the company , and Moscow has said it has no finances to resettle hundreds of thousands of people -- an expenditure which could far outstrip Norilsk 's debts . Norilsk officials declined to comment . Analysts said the government , while anxious about Norilsk 's debts , is highly unlikely to bring the nickel , copper , cobalt , platinum and platinum group metals producer to its knees or take measures that could significantly affect output . But it also wants Norilsk , the world 's second-largest nickel producer , to clean up its act . \\\" The procedure of bankruptcy will be applied , \\\" Tass quoted Livshits as telling Duma deputies about Norilsk . It indirectly quoted him as saying Norilsk should first pay salary arrears , which in the past have led to worker strikes . \\\" It is unlikely that Norilsk will pay these debts in the near-term -- the company will remain a debtor in the near future , \\\" Chernyshev said . He estimated the company 's regional debts at least one trillion roubles and said 30 percent of the giant Krasnoyarsk regional budget was fuelled by Norilsk money . Norilsk 's new majority shareholder , Russian commerical bank Uneximbank , has said it is reorganising metal exports through Interrosimpex in order to boost revenues . But the changes have yet to improve significantly Norilsk 's situation . \\\" Uneximbank has inherited a mountain and whether or not they climb out and over it remains to be seen , \\\" said one metals source . Norilsk said in September that it total debts , including unpaid salaries to workers , were 13 trillion roubles . The company said last month that it had worked out a tax payment schedule with authorities , after regional tax officials threatened to seize some nickel and copper assets . -- Moscow Newsroom , +7095 941 8520\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russia\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 6]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"MOSCOW\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [71, 77]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [89, 96]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Norilsk Nickel\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [161, 175]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norilsk_Nickel\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Moscow\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [442, 448]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Itar-Tass\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [578, 587]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/TASS\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Moscow\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [945, 951]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1087, 1094]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"International Monetary Fund\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1149, 1176]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/International_Monetary_Fund\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Moscow\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1276, 1282]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russia\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1336, 1342]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Moscow\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1707, 1713]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Krasnoyarsk\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [2715, 2726]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Krasnoyarsk_Krai\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [2812, 2819]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Estonian Tallinna Pank 11-mo net 46.6 mln kroons . TALLINN 1996-12-06 Tallinna Pank , one of the largest banks in Estonia , made a 11-month 1996 net profit of 46.6 million kroons , the bank said on Friday . It said in a statement that it made profits of 4.5 million kroons in November . The bank made a profit of 20.1 million kroons in the first half of the year . Tallinna Pank said its assets rose 17.8 million kroons to 1.84 billion kroons . Demand deposits rose to 855.8 million kroons from 834.6 million kroons and time deposits increased to 295.1 million kroons from 285.3 million kroons . -- Riga Newsroom , +371 721 5240\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Estonian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 8]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"TALLINN\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [51, 58]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tallinn\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Estonia\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [114, 121]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Russia ready for constructive work with Albright . MOSCOW 1996-12-06 Russia said on Friday it expected a constructive relationship with Madeleine Albright , nominated by U.S. President Bill Clinton to be Secretary of State . Interfax news agency quoted First Deputy Foreign Minister Igor Ivanov as saying Moscow was ready for \\\" most active and constructive \\\" work with Albright . But he noted that policy would be shaped by Clinton and President Boris Yeltsin . Clinton and Yeltsin are due to meet next March for their first summit since both were re-elected . \\\" Our countries ' leaders have agreed to meet in March , 1997 . The Russian foreign ministry believes the new directions in the development of Russian-U.S. relations will be worked out there , \\\" Ivanov told Interfax . Interfax , outlining Albright 's biography , pointed out that she had defended Washington 's interests fiercely as U.S. ambassador to the United Nations and that this had included actively supporting NATO 's plans to expand eastwards . Russia opposes NATO 's plans to take in countries of eastern and central Europe which used to be part of the Soviet-led Warsaw Pact , saying such moves would threaten its security .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russia\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 6]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Albright\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [40, 48]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Madeleine_Albright\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"MOSCOW\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [51, 57]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Moscow\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Russia\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [69, 75]}, \"target_uri