": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Major\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Major\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [686, 691]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Major\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Clarke\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [696, 702]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenneth_Clarke\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Two dead after executive jet crashes in Newfoundland . STEPHENVILLE , Newfoundland 1996-12-06 Two people were killed when an executive jet en route to Ireland from Michigan crashed on approach to an airport in Stephenville , Newfoundland , on Friday , authorities said . The pilot and co-pilot , the only two aboard , were killed in the crash of the Learjet 36 , airport manager David Snow said in a telephone interview . Snow said the plane last reported to air traffic control at about 3 A.M. local time / 1:30 A.M. EST ( 0630 GMT ) when it began its final approach about 10 miles ( 16 km ) from the airport in this east coast Canadian province . That was the last communication the aircraft made with the airport , he added . \\\" We considered it as being missing until about 0600 ( 4:30 A.M. EST ) ( 0930 GMT ) . That 's when the wreckage was discovered , \\\" Snow said . He said the cargo flight originated in Grand Rapids , Michigan , and was due to stop at Stephenville for refueling before going to Shannon , Ireland . The cause of the crash was not yet known . Investigators were due to fly to Stephenville later on Friday .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Newfoundland\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [40, 52]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Newfoundland_(island)\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Newfoundland\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tupl