\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Michael_Heseltine\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Conservative\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1371, 1383]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Conservative_Party_(UK)\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Edwina Currie\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1387, 1400]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Edwina_Currie\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"BBC\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1410, 1413]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/BBC\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Clarke\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1422, 1428]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenneth_Clarke\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Court ejects head of Australian child-sex inquiry . CANBERRA 1996-12-06 The Australian opposition on Friday demanded a high-powered investigation into paedophilia in the Australian diplomatic service after the federal court forced the head of the existing inquiry to stand aside . The court said inquiry head Chris Hunt might be biased , since he privately told a newspaper he had turned up no major evidence of paedophile activity , even though he still had months ' of investigation before him . \\\" Today we are left with a ruinous wreck beyond salvage and a continuing pall of doubt and suspicion hanging over our diplomatic service , \\\" opposition foreign affairs spokesman Laurie Brereton said . But the government responded by pressing ahead with the original inquiry , established in May , appointing a new head to lead it . Critics say that if there were many paedophiles in senior posts in the Foreign Affairs Department then a secret inquiry would be open to internal influence and would become a public service whitewash . Accordingly , they demand an open investigation . A spokesman for Foreign Affairs Minister Alexander Downer said the appointment of a new inquiry head , administrative law expert Pamela O'Neil , showed the government 's commitment to pursue the matter . A report is due in May next year . One Australian diplomat has been prosecuted this year for having sex with a Cambodian boy under 16 but was acquitted . Police have investigated others . A newspaper reported allegations in April that diplomats had directed Australian government aid to certain foreign orphanages to secure sex with children .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [21, 31]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"CANBERRA\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [52, 60]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canberra\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [76, 86]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [170, 180]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Laurie Brereton\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [676, 691]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Laurie_Brereton\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Foreign Affairs\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1098, 1113]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Minister_for_Foreign_Affairs_(Australia)\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Alexander Downer\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1123, 1139]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Alexander_Downer\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1325, 1335]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Cambodian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1397, 1406]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cambodia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [1544, 1554]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"Australian hitman killed wrong victim . SYDNEY 1996-12-06 An Australian hitman who went to the wrong house and killed the wrong man was sentenced to 20 years jail on Friday . Paul Crofts , 33 , and an accomplice were contracted to shoot a man , identified only as Tony , in the leg to punish him for his misconduct with a female friend of the contractor , the New South Wales Supreme Court was told . But in February 1993 Leszic Betcher , was shot and killed after answering a knock at the door of his Sydney home . \\\" The inference from all the material is that the marauders had come to the wrong house , \\\" Judge Michael Grove said . In sentencing Crofts , who pleaded guilty , Grove took into account his \\\" mildly retarded \\\" intellectual state , which placed him in the lowest two percent of the population . Grove said Betcher was \\\" not only the victim of a horrendous crime , but his death was brought about in circumstances of an equally ghastly error on the part of the prisoner and his accomplices \\\" . The unnamed accomplice was earlier sentenced to 20 years in prison .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 10]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"SYDNEY\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [40, 46]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sydney\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [61, 71]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"New South Wales Supreme Court\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [360, 389]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Supreme_Court_of_New_South_Wales\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Sydney\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [502, 508]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sydney\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"NZ 's Bolger says Nats to meet NZ First on Sunday . WELLINGTON 1996-12-06 New Zealand Prime Minister Jim Bolger , emerging from coalition talks with the nationalist New Zealand First party on Friday afternoon , said National and NZ First would meet again on Sunday . Bolger said he expected a government to be formed by Thursday .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Bolger\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [6, 12]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jim_Bolger\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"WELLINGTON\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [52, 62]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wellington\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"New Zealand\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [74, 85]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Jim Bolger\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [101, 111]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jim_Bolger\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"New Zealand First\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [165, 182]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand_First\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"National\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [216, 224]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand_National_Party\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"NZ First\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [229, 237]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand_First\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Bolger\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [267, 273]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jim_Bolger\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"NZ 's Peters says Nat , Lab talks at similar stage . WELLINGTON 1996-12-06 New Zealand First leader Winston Peters on Friday said coalition talks with the National and Labour parties were at a similar level of completion . Peters left a meeting between NZ First and National negotiators to spend 20 minutes speaking to Labour leader Helen Clark . He told Reuters he had needed to speak to her before she left Wellington later on Friday . Peters said the talks with Labour and National had reached \\\" about the same level of completion , and that 's good \\\" .\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Peters\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [6, 12]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Winston_Peters\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"WELLINGTON\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [53, 63]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wellington\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"sur