http://dbpedia.org/resource/Reuters\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Wellington\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [409, 419]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wellington\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Peters\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [438, 444]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Winston_Peters\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Labour\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [465, 471]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand_Labour_Party\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"National\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [476, 484]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand_National_Party\"}]}, {\"py/object\": \"data.text.TestText\", \"text\": \"RTRS - Australian MP John Langmore formally resigns . CANBERRA 1996-12-06 Australian parliamentarian John Langmore has formally resigned from his lower house seat , the office of House of Representatives speaker Bob Halverson said on Friday . \\\" Halverson announced that he had received today from Mr John Vance Langmore , a letter resigning his place as member of the House of Representatives for the electoral division of Fraser in the Australian Capital Territory , \\\" his office said in a statement . Halverson was considering possible dates for the by-election , his office said . Langmore , 57 , announced in November that he intended to resign from parliament to take up a position as Australia 's senior representative at the United Nations headquarters in New York . He played an active role at the U.N. social development conference in Copenhagen last year and has co-authored articles with U.N. development programme officer Inge Kaul . Langmore , a persistent campaigner for interventionist economic policy , has been Labor member for Fraser since 1984 . He was senior private secretary to the employment and industrial relations minister from 1983 to 1984 and was economic advisor to then treasurer Paul Keating in 1983 . His previous posts include assistant director of the national planning office of Papua New Guinea from 1969 to 1973 . -- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730\", \"entity_mentions\": [{\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"RTRS\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [0, 4]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Radio_and_Television_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [7, 17]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"John Langmore\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [21, 34]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Langmore\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"CANBERRA\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [54, 62]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canberra\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Australian\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [74, 84]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"John Langmore\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [101, 114]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/John_Langmore\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Bob Halverson\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [212, 225]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bob_Halverson\"}, {\"py/object\": \"data.entity.TestEntity\", \"surface_form\": \"Halverson\", \"ner_class\": \"\", \"position\": {\"py/tuple\": [245, 254]}, \"target_uri\": \"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bob_Halverson\"}, {\"py/object